2. Use Case Specifications
UC01 — Learner Registration
Actor: Learner
Goal: Create a learner account.
Preconditions
The learner does not already have an account.
The registration page is available.
Main Flow
Learner opens the registration page.
Learner enters the required personal/account information.
Learner submits the registration form.
System validates the information.
System checks whether the account already exists.
System creates the learner account.
System confirms successful registration.
Learner can proceed to login.
Alternative Flow
If required information is missing or invalid, the system displays an error message.
If the account already exists, the system informs the learner and does not create a duplicate account.
Postconditions
A valid learner account has been created.

UC02 — User Login
Actors: Learner, Assessor, Admin
Goal: Access the system using valid credentials.
Preconditions
The user has an active account.
The user has valid login credentials.
Main Flow
User opens the login page.
User enters their username/email and password.
User selects Login.
System validates the credentials.
System authenticates the user.
System opens the appropriate dashboard.
Alternative Flow
If the credentials are incorrect, the system displays an error message.
The user can try logging in again.
Postconditions
The authenticated user is taken to the appropriate dashboard.

UC03 — Manage Tasks
Actor: Learner
Goal: Manage learning tasks.
Preconditions
Learner is logged in.
Main Flow
Learner opens the task section.
System displays the learner's tasks.
Learner can create a task.
Learner enters the task information.
System saves the task.
Learner can update the task when necessary.
Learner can mark a task as completed.
Learner can choose to delete a task.
System displays a confirmation message.
Learner confirms the deletion.
System removes the task.
Alternative Flow
If the learner cancels the deletion, the task remains unchanged.
If task information is invalid, the system displays an error message.
Postconditions
The task information is successfully created, updated, completed or deleted.
Important:
Tasks do not include due dates, priority or overdue status.

UC04 — View Progress
Actor: Learner
Goal: Monitor learning/task progress.
Preconditions
Learner is logged in.
Learner has tasks or learning activities recorded in the system.
Main Flow
Learner opens the progress section.
System retrieves the learner's task information.
System calculates the percentage of completed tasks.
System displays the learner's progress.
Learner reviews their progress.
Postconditions
The learner can see their current progress.
Progress calculation:
Progress % = (Number of completed tasks ÷ Total number of tasks) × 100
The system does not use points to calculate progress.

UC05 — Access Learning Resources
Actors: Learner, Assessor
Goal: Allow learners to access useful learning materials.
Preconditions
User is logged in.
Learning resources are available.
Main Flow
Learner opens the Resources section.
System displays available learning resources.
Learner selects a resource.
System displays or opens the resource.
Learner uses the resource for learning.
Assessor Flow
Assessor logs in.
Assessor opens the Resources section.
Assessor adds or manages appropriate learning resources.
System saves the changes.
Resources become available to learners.
Postconditions
Learners can access available resources.
Assessor-managed resources are stored in the system.

UC06 — Search and Filter
Actors: Learner, Assessor
Goal: Find relevant information quickly.
Preconditions
User is logged in.
Information is available in the relevant section.
Main Flow
User opens the relevant section.
User enters a search term or selects a filter.
System processes the search/filter.
System displays matching results.
User selects the required information.
Alternative Flow
If no matching results are found, the system displays a suitable message.
Postconditions
User can locate relevant information more easily.

UC07 — Request Learner Support
Actor: Learner
Supporting Actor: Assessor
Goal: Allow learners to request assistance.
Preconditions
Learner is logged in.
Main Flow
Learner opens the Support section.
Learner enters their support request.
Learner submits the request.
System records the request.
Assessor accesses the support request.
Assessor reviews the learner's request.
Assessor provides appropriate assistance.
System records the response where applicable.
Alternative Flow
If the support request is incomplete, the system asks the learner to provide the required information.
Postconditions
The support request has been submitted and can be handled by the Assessor.

UC08 — Play Educational Mini-Game
Actor: Learner
Goal: Participate in an educational activity.
Preconditions
Learner is logged in.
The mini-game is available.
Main Flow
Learner opens the Mini-Game section.
System loads the game.
Learner starts the game.
System presents the game activity/questions.
Learner interacts with the game.
System processes the learner's answers/actions.
System displays the result.
Learner can choose to play again or return to the dashboard.
Postconditions
The learner completes an educational game session.

UC09 — Create Assessor Account
Actor: Admin
Goal: Create an account for an Assessor.
Preconditions
Admin is authenticated.
Admin has permission to manage assessor accounts.
Main Flow
Admin logs into the system.
Admin opens the Assessor Management section.
Admin selects Create Assessor Account.
Admin enters the required assessor information.
System validates the information.
System creates the assessor account.
System generates/stores the assessor's login credentials.
Admin provides the credentials to the Assessor.
Alternative Flow
If the information is invalid, the system displays an error.
If an account already exists, the system prevents a duplicate account.
Postconditions
An Assessor account is created.
The Assessor can use the provided credentials to log in.
Important:
The Assessor does not self-register.

UC10 — Manage Assessor Access
Actor: Admin
Goal: Control assessor access to the system.
Preconditions
Admin is logged in.
An Assessor account exists.
Main Flow
Admin opens Assessor Management.
System displays assessor accounts.
Admin selects an assessor account.
Admin reviews the account information.
Admin can manage the assessor's access.
System saves the changes.
Postconditions
Assessor access is updated according to the Admin's action.

